The multiple regression equation (clean & color‑coded)

\[
\color{var(--accent)}{\Large Y}
\;=\;
\color{var(--muted)}{a}
\;+\;
\color{var(--b1)}{b_1 X_1}
\;+\;
\color{var(--b2)}{b_2 X_2}
\;+\;\cdots+\;
\color{var(--bp)}{b_p X_p}
\]



Legend - (,Y,): outcome (DV)
- (a): intercept (constant)
- (b_j): unstandardised slope for (X_j)
- (X_j): predictor (IV)


Use this when first introducing the model; next slide reveals pieces step‑by‑step.

The same equation, revealed one piece at a time


